  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fact finding study: Small and medium enterprises access to finance Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project provides up-to-date information related to:1)	The financial instruments available for Ukrainian small and medium enterprises (SMEs) from the Ukrainian (UA) government, International Financial Institution, Multilateral Organizations and donors. 2)	The situation of the SMEs -per sector, their knowledge about opportunities for access to finance and their readiness to engage in the economic recovery of Ukraine by making use of the available financial instruments, and identifying concrete needs for accessing to finance. Furthermore, it provides the design of a tailormade training on access to finance matching the needs of the SMEs of the prioritized economic sectors, in line with the Ukrainian Facility Plan, and the criteria of the Ukrainian Investment Framework (UIF) and the available financial instruments in the country. This project is in line with the strategy of the Ukrainian government to boost the local economy and foster the economic recovery of the country in the current war scenario. The project has a positive impact on SDG 8: inclusive and sustainable economic growth: support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation.</narrative>
  </description>
